cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use llm-matmeta in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-matmeta: hybrid rule-based and LLM metadata extraction for computational materials science"
abstract: >-
  llm-matmeta turns the semi-structured output of DFT codes (VASP, Quantum ESPRESSO) and the
  unstructured text of paper abstracts into validated, machine-readable metadata (JSON and
  JSON-LD). Exact rule-based parsers produce a trusted draft, a large language model reads
  condensed evidence into schema-validated JSON, and the two are merged with per-field
  provenance and an explicit list of conflicts, giving FAIR records with ontology mapping.
  Local open-weight models are supported.
type: software
